<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04AK">Example <span data-tag="04AK">8.1.10.8</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="04AH" href="/tag/04AH">8.1.10.6</a>, suppose that $L$ is the collection of all isomorphisms in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then condition $(1)$ is equivalent to the requirement that $U$ is an isofibration (Example <a data-tag="04A3" href="/tag/04A3">8.1.9.8</a>), and condition $(3)$ is automatic. Similarly, if $R$ is the collection of all isomorphisms in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, then condition $(2)$ is the requirement that $U$ is an isofibration, and condition $(3)$ is automatic. </p>
